  "evidence": [
    {
      "sourceId": "src-ad21f0f169fc7912",
      "quote": "Daniels Cardiovascular Biomarkers Lab Lori B. Daniels, MD, MAS, FACC, FAHA, FESC is a Professor of Medicine, Director of the Cardiovascular Intensive Care Unit, and Program Director of the Cardiovascular Disease Fellowship at UC San Diego. She leads the UCSD Cardiovascular Biomarkers Lab within the Division of Cardiovascular Medicine, Sulpizio Cardiovascular Center. Our research focuses on cardiovascular biomarkers and their application to improving risk prediction, diagnosis, and clinical decision‑making in cardiovascular disease. We work on: High‑sensitivity cardiac troponin and natriuretic peptide testing in acute care. Biomarker‑based approaches to screening and prevention. Novel prevention tools such as breast arterial calcification on mammography— a sex‑specific marker of cardiovascular risk. Other emerging biomarkers that bridge discovery and bedside implementation. We emphasize clinically grounded, translational research that connects biomarker discovery and implementation with better patient care for both stable and critically ill cardiovascular patients. Lori B. Daniels, MD, MAS, FACC, FAHA, FESC Professor of Medicine Director, Cardiovascular Intensive Care Unit Program Director, Cardiovascular Disease Fellowship UC San Diego Division of Cardiovascular Medicine Academic Profile | Clinical Profile Biomarkers and Personalized Medicine in Cardiovascular Disease Symposium",
